diff --git a/docs/source/whats_new.rst b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
index e0bfa9e8a0..605842b5c6 100644
--- a/docs/source/whats_new.rst
+++ b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
@@ -103,6 +103,7 @@ Bugs
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.Chang2025` silently skipping subjects 10, 15, 19, 20, 24 and 25 on a fresh download ("Subject directory for S211 not found ... Skipping"): the figshare ZIPs are split by original subject ID (S201-S230, without S207 and S218), but the loader chose the ZIP by MOABB subject number, so these six subjects fetched the neighbouring ZIP and returned no data unless the next subject had been loaded first. The ZIP is now chosen by original ID. Results computed with these subjects missing should be recomputed (:gh:`1284` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - The NEMAR sourcedata prefetch of :meth:`~moabb.datasets.base.BaseDataset.get_data` now also fetches the files a deposit's provenance attributes to no subject (montages, band and interval definitions, shared tables), which every subject's load reads: before, a per-subject prefetch skipped them and the loader fetched them from the upstream host, e.g. :class:`~moabb.datasets.Brandl2020`'s ``mnt.mat`` from DepositOnce with the default ``"auto"`` provider, or failed under ``"nemar"``. A store that lacks them is no longer reported as complete (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Archive-based loaders no longer download the archive when NEMAR already served its contents: NEMAR deposits mirror the extracted members, not the ``.zip``, so the URL lookup in :func:`moabb.datasets.download.data_dl` could not match and :class:`~moabb.datasets.BI2012`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.BI2014a`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.BI2014b`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.BI2015a`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.BI2015b`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.BNCI2019_001`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.BNCI2025_001` and :class:`~moabb.datasets.Hinss2021` fetched the whole archive from the upstream host even with the default ``"auto"`` provider. They now ask the new :func:`moabb.datasets.download.fill_from_store` for the members they read (located with the new :func:`~moabb.datasets.download.data_dl_destination`) and download only when the store lacks one of them; members are linked all-or-nothing, so a partial deposit never leaves a half-extracted tree (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- :class:`moabb.datasets.Huebner2017`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Huebner2018`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Liu2024` and :class:`moabb.datasets.Sosulski2019` no longer download the Zenodo ``subjectXX.zip`` / figshare ``edffile.zip`` / FreiDok archive when NEMAR (``nm000199``, ``nm000195``, ``nm000158``, ``nm000266``) or an earlier extraction already holds the files they read: ``data_path`` now looks for the extracted subject directory (Huebner, Sosulski2019) or EDF (Liu2024) first, through :func:`moabb.datasets.download.fill_from_store` and the new :func:`moabb.datasets.download.fill_tree_from_store`, which places a whole extracted directory from the store and refuses one whose BrainVision/EEGLAB headers name files the store lacks. Liu2024 now extracts only the archive members not on disk yet, so a later extraction does not write through the links into the NEMAR store, and Sosulski2019 extracts the archive again when a subject's inner ZIP is missing instead of whenever ``extracted/`` is absent (:gh:`1293` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`~moabb.datasets.Nieto2022` and :class:`~moabb.datasets.TrianaGuzman2024` declared their NEMAR raw mirrors (``on003626``, ``on005342``) but always downloaded from OpenNeuro's S3 bucket; like the other OpenNeuro loaders they now read the mirror first under the ``"auto"`` and ``"nemar"`` providers and keep OpenNeuro as the fallback and for ``"upstream"`` (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`~moabb.datasets.Chailloux2020`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.Nieto2022` and :class:`~moabb.datasets.TrianaGuzman2024` declared their NEMAR raw mirrors (``on003190``, ``on003626``, ``on005342``) but always downloaded from OpenNeuro's S3 bucket; like the other OpenNeuro loaders they now read the mirror first under the ``"auto"`` and ``"nemar"`` providers and keep OpenNeuro as the fallback and for ``"upstream"`` (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.Peterson2020` loads again with the default ``"auto"`` download provider: the NEMAR mirror (``on003810``) ships the BIDS ``events.tsv`` sidecars, so ``read_raw_bids`` replaced the EDF's ``OVTK_GDF_Right``/``OVTK_GDF_Tongue`` annotations with the sidecar values ``7``/``9`` and every load stopped with ``ValueError: Could not find any of the events you specified``. Both codings now map to ``motor_imagery``/``rest`` (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
